aine  using new american delivered weapons  rocket artillery systems highmars is the  name to attack  russian logistics hubs russian weapons  depots to basically deprive russia of  that huge advantage it's been having and  taking advantage of in recent weeks and  months of just having seven to ten times  more artillery systems their disposal at  least that's those the figures that the  ukrainians have been uh talking of so  basically they're trying to starve the  russian positions in gerson region which  are already a lot less well equipped  than the russian positions in the east  of the country ahead of them trying to  make some ground and push forward and  really  you know start making progress and  taking more territory for the first time  in in a couple of months and as that  fighting continues nick the united  nations has released new numbers on the  human toll of the war and i'd just like  to um to walk us through some of them  they say that more than 5 million people  have been displaced at least 5 000  civilians killed saying that that number  is actually likely much higher  walk us through how people in ukraine  are coping nearly half a year now into  this war  it is amazing how this country has  continued functioning how the trains  kept running how mobile for phone  connections have been restored after  infrastructure has been destroyed time  and time again no no issue with  electricity for now basic services  available here in kiev certainly but  also places pretty close to the front  lines obviously in donbass closest to  where those artillery battles have been  going on some people have been left  without power without  internet for weeks now but overall the  country is  managing to stand up a lot better than  anyone had it managed but it is now  obviously  after so many months of fighting taking  its toll and there is the question is  how long can individual families  individual uh ukrainians carry on often  without jobs often living off their  saving